data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

In .NET 10, the Cosmos DB provider **deprecated** synchronous query execution and made sync-over-async opt-in via `CosmosOptionsExtension`. In **.NET 11 (EF Core 11), that opt-in is removed entirely**. Synchronous LINQ operators on the Cosmos provider now **throw `InvalidOperationException`** — there is no flag to re-enable them.

### Affected calls in your code

| Method | Why it breaks |
|---|---|
| `.ToList()` | Sync enumeration removed |
| `.First(...)` | Sync evaluation removed |
| `.Count()` | Sync evaluation removed |
| `.SaveChanges()` | Sync persist removed |

### Fix: switch to async equivalents

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `Add()` is still synchronous (it only tracks in-memory) — no change needed there.
- All callers up the stack must also become `async`/`await` (controllers, services, etc.).
- Remove the old `EnableSyncOverAsync()` / sync-over-async opt-in configuration — it no longer compiles.
